# tests/ is excluded wholesale because the build context must not carry the test
# suite into the image. welcome-close-gate.sh is the one exception: it is a gate
# that runs against the INSTALLED system, so it has to ship, and it stays under
# tests/ because it is a test and must keep reading like one. Verified with a
# scratch build that this negation re-includes exactly this file and nothing
# else from tests/.
!tests/welcome-close-gate.sh

# The DN-48 LibreOffice parity gates, same reasoning. The .xcd checker runs at
# build time, and the UNO gate and its probe cannot: there is no LibreOffice to
# start inside a build layer, so they ship to be run against the installed
# system on the Dell or a VM, which is the only place the parity is real.
!tests/libreoffice-xcd-check.py
!tests/libreoffice-parity-gate.sh
!tests/libreoffice-parity-probe.py

# The Help application's gate, same reasoning again: it needs the help server
# running and a browser engine to drive, neither of which exists inside a build
# layer, so it ships to be run against the installed system.
!tests/help-app-gate.sh
!tests/help-app-probe.py

# The update-lane guard gate. Unlike the ones above it does NOT ship: it runs at
# build time against spplus-update-control and is deleted in the same RUN layer.
# It is only re-included here so the COPY has something to copy -- tests/ is
# excluded wholesale above, and that exclusion silently failed the build on
# 2026-09-01 at STEP 54 with "no items matching glob ... (1 filtered out)".
!tests/update-guard-gate.sh
!tests/update-lane-gate.sh

# The five Fin gates and the permissions probe. Four of the five gates run at
# build time AND ship, so an advisor's machine can be checked against the same
# assertions later; the probe is data the permissions gate executes.
#
# This is the THIRD time tests/ being excluded wholesale has failed a build at a
# COPY -- 2026-09-01 at STEP 54 (update-guard-gate, recorded above) and again on
# 2026-09-12 at STEP 39 building v0.11.1, which is what added these six lines.
# The pattern is not that people forget: it is that adding a COPY and adding the
# negation are two edits in two files, and only the second one is invisible until
# a twenty-minute build dies. tests/config-preflight.sh now applies this file to
# every COPY source so the failure arrives in two seconds instead.
!tests/fin-notebook-gate.sh
!tests/fin-skills-gate.sh
!tests/fin-session-meter-gate.sh
!tests/fin-opening-gate.sh
!tests/fin-permissions-gate.sh
!tests/fin-permissions-probe.cjs
